{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Send me away, that I may go.</b> For even though he did not then have acquired flocks in hand — since his wages had passed by means of his staff — he did have enough to sustain his wives and children, at the least enough to buy bread and clothing and provisions for the journey. For otherwise it would not befit a righteous and wise man to desire to go forth to death and to cause death by starvation. Nor would it enter his mind that Laban, who was wealthy and honored in his city, would agree to send off his daughters and his daughters' children to kill the entire company by hunger, thirst, and nakedness on a long journey. And so Laban pleaded with him to remain with him for his own advantage, as he said: <b>YHWH has blessed me for your sake</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:36.816025518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}